      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> A compliant gabion basket uses hexagonal double-twist mesh with 60 × 80, 80 × 100, or 100 × 120 mm openings, body wire of 2.2–2.7 mm and selvedge (edge) wire of 3.0–4.0 mm, coated in one of three systems: hot-dip galvanized (cheapest, ~2–10 year life), GALFAN zinc-5%-aluminum (best value, ~2–3× the corrosion life of plain zinc), or PVC-coated over galvanized wire (longest life, 50+ year claims in mild environments). FOB China pricing runs roughly $12–25/m³ for standard galvanized, $15–32/m³ for GALFAN, and $22–45/m³ for PVC-coated, depending on wire diameter and zinc class. Specify internal diaphragms every 1 m, matching lids, and 3% lacing wire — then insist on a filled-and-braced installation sequence, because 90% of gabion failures are installation failures, not material failures. Full specs, price tables, and the installation sequence are below.
      </p>
